powerpc/powernv: export opal_npu_init_context()/opal_npu_destroy_context()

Patch 0001 restored the OPAL_CALL() wrappers for OPAL_NPU_INIT_CONTEXT and
OPAL_NPU_DESTROY_CONTEXT and their prototypes in <asm/opal.h>, but did not
export them.  They therefore exist as vmlinux symbols with no __ksymtab
entry and cannot be reached from a module.

Export both as GPL symbols so that a module -- an out-of-tree GPU driver, or
a future in-tree NPU2 module -- can arm and tear down the nest MMU
translation context for an NVLink-attached GPU.

The exports are placed in opal.c rather than opal-call.c because that is
where every other OPAL symbol in this tree is exported from; the OPAL_CALL()
macro in opal-call.c only emits the function body.  EXPORT_SYMBOL* does not
have to live in the same translation unit as the definition, and
opal_xscom_read()/opal_flash_read()/etc. are already handled this way.

Risk: minimal.  Additive only; no behavioural change to anything already
in the tree.  Worst case is two extra ksymtab entries.

Derived from: no direct v5.12 equivalent (v5.12 did not export these either
-- the in-kernel caller pnv_npu2_init_context() lived in the same object).
This is new, and deliberate.

---

--- a/arch/powerpc/platforms/powernv/opal.c
+++ b/arch/powerpc/platforms/powernv/opal.c
@@ -1243,3 +1243,12 @@
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(opal_error_code);
 /* Export the below symbol for NX compression */
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(opal_nx_coproc_init);
+/*
+ * Export the NPU2 (NVLink2) context calls so that out-of-tree GPU drivers
+ * and any future in-tree module can arm the nest MMU translation context
+ * for an NVLink-attached GPU. These are plain OPAL wrappers generated by
+ * OPAL_CALL() in opal-call.c; like the other OPAL symbols above they are
+ * exported from here.
+ */
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(opal_npu_init_context);
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(opal_npu_destroy_context);
